Pipkin Quickspark, a gnome warlock barely taller than a raptor, adjusted his goggles as he and Seraphina, his succubus familiar, navigated the dense foliage of Stranglethorn Vale. "Right, Seraphina," he squeaked, consulting his quest log. "Five raptor hides. Seduction should make this *much* easier than fighting them head-on."

Seraphina, lounging elegantly on a giant mushroom, rolled her eyes. "Must you always be so… predictable, Pipkin? A little brute force would be refreshing."

Pipkin ignored her, spotting a trio of raptors. With a flourish, Seraphina unleashed Seduction, momentarily charming the beasts into a confused dance. Pipkin, meanwhile, frantically stuffed hides into his bag, dodging a frustrated peck from one of the now-un-charmed raptors. "Almost... got it!" he cried, narrowly escaping a snapping beak. "Just one more!"



The answer is: **Voidwalkers provided significantly more threat generation, making them essential for soloing higher-level content and dealing with multiple enemies, despite the succubus's damage advantage.** [end of text]


